{:edb/db-before-t 2537 :edb/db-after-t 2538 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535850 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:56:17.161Z" 13194139535850 true] [17592186051845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370045 13194139535850 true] [17592186051845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370046 13194139535850 true] [17592186051845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370045 13194139535850 true] [17592186051856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370055 13194139535850 true] [17592186051864 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370067 13194139535850 true] [17592186051864 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370067 13194139535850 true] [17592186054737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370047 13194139535850 true] [17592186054737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370068 13194139535850 true] [17592186054738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370038 13194139535850 true] [17592186054738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370075 13194139535850 true] [17592186054739 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370052 13194139535850 true] [17592186054739 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370056 13194139535850 true] [17592186054739 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370060 13194139535850 true] [17592186054740 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370064 13194139535850 true] [17592186054987 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535850 true] [17592186054987 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nIf $A = {3, 6, 12, 24, 48, …, 98304}$, then $\\mid A|=$ {{field-1}}." 13194139535850 false] [17592186054987 1100 "If $A={3,6,12,24,48,…,98\\,304},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." 13194139535850 true] [17592186054987 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=3({2}^{n-1})=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{N} & =98\\,304 \\\\ {2}^{N} & =65\\,536 \\\\ N & ={log}_{2}⁡(65\\,536) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(65\\,536)}{{log}_{10}⁡(2)} \\\\ N & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $16$ elements, we must have $|A|=16.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186054996 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535850 true] [17592186054996 1100 "If $X = {{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, {1, 2, 3, 4}, ∅}$, then $\\mid X|=$ {{field-1}}." 13194139535850 false] [17592186054996 1100 "If $X={{1,2,3,4,5},{1,2,3,4},∅}$, then $|X|=${{field-1}}." 13194139535850 true] [17592186054996 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\n{1,2,3,4,5},\\,{1,2,3,4},\\,∅\n$$\n\nNote that ${1,2,3,4,5},$ ${1,2,3,4},$ and $∅$ each count as single elements of $X.$\n\nSince $X$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|X|=3.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186306088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370050 13194139535850 true] [17592186306094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370051 13194139535850 true] [17592186306116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370063 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370039 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1089 "q-104909" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1100 "If $A={1,{10,12},15,{22,26,28},{42,62}}$, then $|A|=$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1113 #uuid "2fcc379f-2f4b-5f54-bdd5-04d5716c1760" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370038 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,{10,12},\\,15,\\,{22,26,28},\\,{42,62}\n$$\n\nNote that ${10,12},$ ${22,26,28},$ and ${42,62}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ ha