1f-5a68-95c6-b3470ada6ae8" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370052 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n98,\\,102,\\,106,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4 \\\\  & =102-98 \\\\  & =106-102 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =98+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =98+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+94.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4N+94 & =810 \\\\ 4N & =716 \\\\ N & =\\frac{716}{4} \\\\ N & =179\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 179}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $179$ elements, we must have $|A|=179.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370053 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370054 13194139535850 true] [17592186370053 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535850 true] [17592186370053 1041 "field-1" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370053 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370054 13194139535850 true] [17592186370053 1110 #uuid "0681fd81-d1a6-552e-9c6f-aa8dcac4d0ca" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370054 1034 "179" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370054 1111 #uuid "a790c782-9db3-5d30-9e7b-5d2b79eb784c" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370055 1034 "171" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370055 1111 #uuid "0a3e3c04-33bc-5e83-8673-861763310039" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370057 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1089 "q-181566" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1100 "If $A={-875,-869,-863,…,6\\,151},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1113 #uuid "359ce01e-7589-5ea5-9246-896c5271d8b4" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370056 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-875,\\,-869,\\,-863,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =6 \\\\  & =-869-(-875) \\\\  & =-863-(-869) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-875+(n-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-875+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n-881.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={6n-881:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6N-881 & =6\\,151 \\\\ 6N & =7\\,032 \\\\ N & =\\frac{7\\,032}{6} \\\\ N & =1\\,172\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={6n-881:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 1\\,172}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $1\\,172$ elements, we must have $|A|=1\\,172.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370058 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370059 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1041 "field-1" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370058 13194139535850 true] [17592186370057 1110 #uuid "0e99bfad-f453-5595-88cd-a12a8cd3134a" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370058 1034 "1172" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370058 1111 #uuid "ca7fe877-2e4b-5b33-902f-eac0d170d910" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370059 1034 "1171" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370059 1111 #uuid "6b939c76-c6b4-54db-a953-2861a40252c2" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370061 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1089 "q-181573" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1100 "If $A={-615,-610,-605,…,12\\,425},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1113 #uuid "b7155e82-f133-5ff9-8973-883ba9513f97" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370060 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-615,\\,-610,\\,-605,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =5 \\\\  & =-610-(-615) \\\\  & =-605-(-610) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-615+(n-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-615+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-620.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={5n-620:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5N-620 & =12\\,425 \\\\ 5N & =13\\,045 \\\\ N & =\\frac{13\\,045}{5} \\\\ N & =2\\,609\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={5n-620:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 2\\,609}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $2\\,609$ elements, we must have $|A|=2\\,609.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370062 13194139535850 true] [17592186370061 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535850 true] [17592186370061 1041 "field-1" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370061 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370062 13194139535850 true] [17592186370061 1110 #uuid "a39118b0-5fdc-5c1a-b0e5-023f16d9c9b4" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370062 1034 "2609" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370062 1111 #uuid "6840236d-565f-5bce-b2bc-e90bb8adfff6" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370063 1034 "13" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535850 true] [17592186370063 1111 #uuid "05ce2efe-1704-5dad-a131-8dd0858ff065" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370065 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1089 "q-181584" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1100 "If $A={1,9,81,729,…,3\\,486\\,784\\,401},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1113 #uuid "b4b82edb-27c4-5eb4-8e21-16aeb96703eb" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370064 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,9,\\,81,\\,729,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{9} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {9}^{n-1}={9}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{9}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{9}^{N-1} & =3\\,486\\,784\\,401 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{9}⁡(3\\,486\\,784\\,401) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(3\\,486\\,784\\,401)}{{log}_{10}⁡(9)} \\\\ N-1 & =10 \\\\ N & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{9}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 11}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $11$ elements, we must have $|A|=11.$" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370065 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370066 13194139535850 true] [17592186370065 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535850 true] [17592186370065 1041 "field-1" 13194139535850 true] [17592186370065 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370066 13194139535850 true] [17592186370065 1110 